{
  "manifest": {
    "id": "ACEE-INVARIANT-MANIFEST-001",
    "name": "Constitutional completion invariant manifest",
    "authority": "NONE — DERIVED TRUTH. This manifest legislates no invariant and satisfies none. It RECORDS, for each constitutional completion invariant, the located owner Repository Truth already shows, the anchor inside that owner which evidences it, and a counter in a committed artifact by which it is measured. The engine then MEASURES: an owner that does not resolve, an anchor that is absent, or a measure that is unmet reports so, and the disposition follows from the measurement. Nothing here asserts that an invariant is satisfied.",
    "open": true,
    "closed_enumeration": false,
    "admission": "Append a node record to `nodes`, or add another manifest matching the located manifest pattern. No engine change, no declaration change, no architectural redesign. The engine never reads this file by name: it is discovered by the declared root and suffix, so a second manifest is admitted by dropping it in.",
    "ordinal_step": 10,
    "$measure_comment": "`measure_source` names a COMMITTED artifact of another owner and `measure` is a dotted pointer into it. No register this programme writes may appear as a measure source: reading back its own output would make a view a source, and the engine fails closed on that.",
    "$anchor_comment": "`anchor` is a literal that must occur inside the owner. It is what stops an owner from being cited for an obligation it does not actually evidence.",
    "$disposition_comment": "Disposition is NOT recorded here. It is derived by the engine from the measurement, because a disposition written by hand would be an assertion and the constitution admits only measurement."
  },
